#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/HA_Shared_Storage.rst:17
msgid ""
"To copy the ``morpheus-ui`` directory to the shared storage follow the "
"below steps:"
msgstr ""
"To copy the ``morpheus-ui`` directory to the almacenamiento compartido "
"follow the abajo steps:"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/HA_Shared_Storage.rst:19
msgid "SSH into the Appliance"
msgstr "SSH en the Appliance"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/HA_Shared_Storage.rst:20
msgid "sudo su (or login as root)"
msgstr "sudo su (or login as root)"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/HA_Shared_Storage.rst:21
msgid "cd into ``/var/opt/morpheus/``"
msgstr "cd en ``/var/opt/morpheus/``"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/HA_Shared_Storage.rst:22
msgid ""
"Backup morpheus-ui directory by running the command below.  This will "
"create a new directory in ``/var/opt/morpheus/`` called morpheus-ui-bkp "
"and copy the contents of morpheus-ui into the new directory"
msgstr ""
"Backup morpheus-ui directory by running the command below. This will "
"create a new directory in ``/var/opt/morpheus/`` called morpheus-ui-bkp y "
"copy the contents of morpheus-ui ina la new directory"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/HA_Shared_Storage.rst:24
#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/HA_Shared_Storage.rst:38
msgid "cp -r morpheus-ui morpheus-ui-bkp"
msgstr "cp -r morpheus-ui morpheus-ui-bkp"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/HA_Shared_Storage.rst:28
msgid "Move morpheus-ui to your shared storage. Example below:"
msgstr "Move morpheus-ui to your almacenamiento compartido. Example below:"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/HA_Shared_Storage.rst:30
msgid "mv morpheus-ui /nfs/appliance-files/"
msgstr "mv morpheus-ui /nfs/appliance-files/"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/HA_Shared_Storage.rst:34
msgid ""
"Mount your shared storage volume to ``/var/opt/morpheus/morpheus-ui``. "
"How you mount it is dependent on what kind of storage it is. If you mount"
" the volume after the package install, but before the reconfigure, then "
"you don't need to copy anything to a backup."
msgstr ""
"Mount your shared storage volume to ``/var/opt/morpheus/morpheus-ui``. How "
"you mount it is dependent on what kind of storage it is. If you mount the "
"volume after the package install, but before the reconfigure, then you "
"don't need to copy anything to a backup."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/HA_Shared_Storage.rst:36
msgid ""
"SSH into the second Appliance and then Backup morpheus-ui directory by "
"running"
msgstr "SSH en the second Appliance y then Backup morpheus-ui directory by running"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/HA_Shared_Storage.rst:42
msgid "When adding additional nodes you will only need to run step 6 and 7"
msgstr "When adding adicional nodes you will only necesita run step 6 y 7"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/HA_Shared_Storage.rst:44
msgid ""
"NFS mounts require ``sync`` option when using Ansible integration with "
"|morpheus| Agent command bus execution enabled."
msgstr ""
"NFS mounts require ``sync`` option when using Ansible integration con "
"|morpheus| Agent command bus execution enabled."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/distributed/HA_Shared_Storage.rst:46
msgid ""
"On each application node, the morpheus-app and morpheus-local user and "
"group uid/gid should be consistent.  If the uid and/or gid are different "
"between nodes, when the permissions are applied during a reconfigure, the"
" permissions can be incorrect for other nodes.  The uid and gid for the "
"users can be seen by executing:  ``sudo cat /etc/passwd`` and ``sudo cat "
"/etc/groups``"
msgstr ""
"On each application node, the morpheus-app y morpheus-local user y group "
"uid/gid debería ser consistent.  If the uid and/or gid are different entre "
"nodes, when the permissions are applied durante a reconfigure, the "
"permissions puede ser incorrect for other nodes.  The uid y gid for los "
"usuarios puede ser seen by executing:  ``sudo cat /etc/passwd`` y ``sudo "
"cat /etc/groups``"

